 \mytriangle{red} Here you can learn how to add the elements of a list:
   \begin{solutionbox} \begin{center}\bf{List addition with Texas TI-84}\end{center}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\protect\circled{\color{white}\arabic*}]
\item \begin{bf}Step one:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{Stat} and \keystroke{Enter}. Type the List 1(L1) values.
\item \begin{bf}Step two:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{mode} to quit from the Stat menu. 
\item \begin{bf}Step three:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{0} to access the catalog.
\item \begin{bf}Step four:\end{bf} Look for the Sum() function. You can press the letter \keystroke{S} or use the arrows up and down to locate the function. When you find the function, press \keystroke{Enter}.
\item \begin{bf}Step five:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{1} to operate with L1. Make sure to close the parenthesis.
\item \begin{bf}Step six:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{Enter} and you will obtain the result of adding all values of L1.
\end{enumerate}
\end{solutionbox}
